---
import SourcePanel from '../components/SourcePanel.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { ASSETS } from '../data/assets';
import { SOURCES } from '../data/sources';

const title = 'Grave Seasons Character Customization - Wearables, Hair & Skin Tones';
const description =
  'Grave Seasons character customization confirmed by the official devlog: 35 wearables, 25 skin tones, 14 clothing colours and 33 ways to colour 18 hairstyles.';
const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Character Customization', url: '/character-customization/' },
];
const sources = [SOURCES.steamDevlog, SOURCES.steam];
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs} image={ASSETS.hari.src}>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <p class="section-kicker">Character - official devlog</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-black leading-tight text-bone md:text-5xl">
      Grave Seasons Character Customization
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-fog">
      Perfect Garbage's dev log confirmed exactly how much customization ships at launch. These are
      official numbers, not estimates.
    </p>

    <figure class="mt-8">
      <img src={ASSETS.hari.src} alt={ASSETS.hari.alt} width={ASSETS.hari.width} height={ASSETS.hari.height} class="rounded-md border border-white/10" loading="lazy" />
      <figcaption class="mt-2 text-xs text-fog">{ASSETS.hari.credit}</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="prose-page mt-8">
      <h2>What you can customize at launch</h2>
      <p>
        Everything in Grave Seasons is hand-made pixel art, so customization is not a menu of
        recoloured presets - each option is drawn and animated by hand. On launch the game will
        include:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>35 unique wearables</strong></li>
        <li><strong>25 skin tone options</strong></li>
        <li>A mix-and-match clothing style setup with <strong>14 colour options</strong></li>
        <li><strong>33 ways to colour 18 different hairstyles</strong></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why it is a big deal (technically)</h2>
      <p>
        Because the game animates in <strong>up to 8 directions</strong>, every wearable has to be
        drawn for each one. The devlog puts real numbers on that effort: each wearable is animated
        into <strong>70+ sprite sheets</strong>, implemented as <strong>over 400 animations</strong>
        that can trigger throughout the game - reacting to a murder, sharing a kiss with a lover,
        passing out from exhaustion. The team even called out their commitment to the "hair bounce."
      </p>

      <h2>What we do not know yet</h2>
      <p>
        The devlog confirms the <em>quantities</em> but not the <em>mechanics</em>: how you unlock
        wearables, whether appearance can be changed freely after creation, and whether any cosmetics
        are tied to romance or story progress are all unconfirmed. We will fill those in from the
        release build rather than guess.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-fog">
        Treat any "best outfit" or unlock-order claim you see elsewhere as speculation until launch.
      </p>

      <h2>Where this fits</h2>
      <p>
        Character customization pairs with the game's heavy narrative focus - 300k+ words and 30+
        residents to build relationships with. For the residents themselves, see the
        <a href="/characters/">character tracker</a>; for relationship routes, the
        <a href="/romance-guide/">romance guide</a>. For how the art team thinks about pixel art -
        and why they treat its limits as a horror advantage - see the
        <a href="/art-style/">art style devlog</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <SourcePanel sources={sources} />
  </article>
</Layout>
